1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
My only love sprung from my only hate.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Romeo + Juliet is a drama, romance film directed by Baz Luhrmann.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
In director Baz Luhrmann's contemporary take on William Shakespeare's classic tragedy, the Montagues and Capulets have moved
their ongoing feud to the sweltering suburb of Verona Beach, where Romeo and Juliet fall in love and secretly wed.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Though the film is visually modern, the bard's dialogue remains.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Romeo, played by Leonardo DiCaprio.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Juliet, played by Claire Danes.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Balthasar, played by Jesse Bradford.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Captain Prince, played by Vondie Curtis-Hall.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Ted Montague, played by Brian Dennehy.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Tybalt, played by John Leguizamo.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
William Shakespeare's Romeo & Juliet (stylized as William Shakespeare's Romeo + Juliet) is a
1996 romantic crime film directed, produced, and co-written by Baz Luhrmann.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
It is a modernized adaptation of William Shakespeare's tragedy of the
same name, albeit still using Shakespearean English.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The film stars Leonardo DiCaprio and Claire Danes in the title roles of two teenagers
who fall in love, despite their being members of feuding families.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Brian Dennehy, John Leguizamo, Miriam Margolyes, Harold Perrineau, Pete
Postlethwaite, Paul Sorvino and Diane Venora also star in supporting roles.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
It is the third major film version of the play, following adaptations by
George Cukor in 1936 and by Franco Zeffirelli in 1968.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film was released on November 1, 1996, by 20th Century Fox.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
It was met with generally positive reviews from critics and grossed
over $147 million against its $14.5 million budget.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
At the 47th Berlin International Film Festival in 1997, DiCaprio won the Silver
Bear for Best Actor and Luhrmann won the Alfred Bauer Prize.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
At the 69th Academy Awards, Catherine Martin and Brigitte Broch
were nominated for Best Art Direction/Set Decoration.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
In 2005, the film was included on the BFI list of the "50
films you should watch by the age of 14".

21
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The film was also re-released in Luhrmann's Red Curtain Trilogy DVD box set in
2002 together with Strictly Ballroom (1992) and Moulin Rouge!

22
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
The film explores themes of suicide, gang war, forbidden
love, based on play or musical, murder.

23
01:55:00,000 --> 01:55:06,000
The tone is emotional.
